rules:
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires all architectural decisions to be expressed using a structured
    YAML decision schema (ADR) rather than unstructured narrative text.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Establishes Architecture Decision Records (ADR) as the single source of
    truth; all other representations must be derived from them.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that all new patterns are created as 'supporting' by default and
    validated through usage before becoming foundational 'core' patterns.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Prohibits the merging or consolidation of patterns across different architectural
    layers to preserve separation of concerns.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the resolution hierarchy for rule conflicts, where Global rules
    act as hard constraints that supersede Project and Prompt-level rules.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures traceability by requiring heuristic-derived patterns to include
    at least one linked signal as grounding evidence.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Enforces consistent mapping between pattern maturity (knowledge evolution)
    and decision status (governance lifecycle) to prevent unvalidated architecture.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: "Defines mandatory criteria\u2014recurrence, impact, reusability, and stability\u2014\
    that a signal must satisfy before promotion to a pattern."
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts must only summarize authoritative source
    data and must not maintain independent or manually introduced state.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires runtime workflows to adhere to the CAS execution model, separating
    orchestration, reasoning, and knowledge provider responsibilities.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that the lifecycle stage of any architectural item must be derived
    from its governance decision status; unaccepted items cannot be marked as DONE.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires projects to participate in a shared workspace and prevents the
    duplication of workspace-level governance structures and assets.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Designates Architecture Work as the authoritative source for planning state,
    ensuring roadmap and map artifacts derive status from it.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures the Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) reflects and does not contradict
    established Architecture Decision Records (ADR).
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains human-in-the-loop governance by requiring all system-proposed
    architectural decisions to be explicitly actioned by an architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures all architectural decisions are persisted as structured ADRs before
    being reflected in visibility tools like the AEM.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Restricts 'core' pattern classification to foundational primitives rather
    than specific implementation strategies or context-specific approaches.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires pattern promotion to core to be supported by strong evidence from
    multiple sources to ensure architectural stability.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines a precise semantic contract for architectural language to ensure
    clarity between intent, state, and governance-approved transitions.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
